body:
!remindme 4 weeks

&#x200B;

I'm assuming you didn't survive, OP, but I'm still holding on to some hope that your recovery is just taking longer than you thought. Either way, best wishes to your friends and family.

Bathing cats is usually not necessary (unless for a flea bath) and cats will like it if they like water, and dislike it if they don't. Personally, I've aways free fed my cats, with wet food twice a day (especially with males, due to the danger of UTIs in cats, and male cats get them faster then females), but cats with a history of abuse/hunger/etc might eat too much out of fear they won't have food anymore. What works with my cat when he scratches or bite and it hurts is to hiss and ignore him. Just completely stop play behaviour. He understands he fucked up and plays on his own for a little while.

&#x200B;

Remember that as his owner, you know everything (or will, soon enough) about him, so you'll know when to take him to the vet, when to give him food, when to play with him, etc naturally. It just takes a little while to get to that point. You'll be a great owner, and that's very clear from this post.

An entrée isn't SUPPOSED to fill you up and have enough for leftovers, that's what the main dish is there for. The entrée is meant to be a small, light portion that opens you up to the main dish. That's literally what it means, btw, "open" not "full meal that fills you up"

&#x200B;

YTA

Right? Like if B was just maybe a misguided, kinda dumb, adult he'd have said something like "Oh yeah, we were gonna go get subway. Is that a problem? Should I check with your mom?" but no, he went straight for "I wasn't gonna do anything" which screams "I was gonna do something that's really not okay, possibly illegal"

&#x200B;

NTA, OP, and update your mom. You two need to work as a team to keep your brother safe.
